Q: How to handle API response in a ViewModel A: <p>Your <code>toDayState</code> function is trying to force every <code>ApiResponse</code> variant into a <code>DayState</code>, which doesn't really make sense — Loading and Error don't have the data needed to construct one. The cleaner approach is to make your UI state reflect all three possibilities explicitly:</p>
<p>kotlin</p>
<pre><code>sealed class DayUiState {
    object Loading : DayUiState()
    data class Success(val dayState: DayState) : DayUiState()
    data class Error(val message: String?) : DayUiState()
}

fun toDayUiState(response: ApiResponse&lt;Day&gt;): DayUiState = when (response) {
    is ApiResponse.Loading -&gt; DayUiState.Loading
    is ApiResponse.Success -&gt; DayUiState.Success(
        DayState(
            date = response.data.date,
            activeTimeStart = response.data.activeTimeStart,
            // ...etc
        )
    )
    is ApiResponse.Error -&gt; DayUiState.Error(response.message)
}
</code></pre>
<p>Your ViewModel then exposes <code>StateFlow&lt;DayUiState&gt;</code> and your UI reacts accordingly — showing a spinner, the data, or an error message.</p>
